      "math_academy_id": "q-95505",
      "knowledge_point_id": "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{e}^{x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{({e}^{x})}^{2}}\\cdot {({e}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{2x}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1-{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
